=== D. Theorem thm:imbalance ===
  identity E_a a_a = 2h<phi_a,V Gamma phi_a> and X_B = 2h sum r_x R(x,B): max err = 1.4e-14
  pointwise |sum_B r| - 2 sum_(B x B^c) R - |X_B|/(2|h|): max = -1.4e-02 (<=0)
  Cauchy-Schwarz and sum_a E_a^2 m_a(B) <= L(2J^2+4h^2): max violation = 1.7e-13 (<=0)
  N=8, h=0.7, all 256 sectors: (1/T)int_0^T I(t)dt (T=1e7, exact) = 0.19046876; E_q N^-1 sum_a a_a^2 = 0.19046877; I(0) = 1.000; |I_q(t) - N^-1 Tr(Gamma U* Gamma U)| = 7.8e-16
  h=0, N=10: max_a |a_a| = 6.9e-16 (Ibar = 0)
  lower bounds (kappa_N = max over all intervals B of E sum_{x in B,y notin B} R; 300 sectors):
    N= 32 lambda=+0.5: Ibar = 0.0298, kappa_N = 5.75, global bound = 1.25e-03, best block bound = 0.00e+00, Ibar >= max: True
    N= 32 lambda=+1.0: Ibar = 0.0920, kappa_N = 3.70, global bound = 3.47e-03, best block bound = 0.00e+00, Ibar >= max: True
    N= 32 lambda=+2.0: Ibar = 0.1844, kappa_N = 2.26, global bound = 7.81e-03, best block bound = 0.00e+00, Ibar >= max: True
    N= 32 lambda=+4.0: Ibar = 0.2556, kappa_N = 1.91, global bound = 1.39e-02, best block bound = 1.31e-05, Ibar >= max: True
    N= 32 lambda=-1.8: Ibar = 0.1727, kappa_N = 2.32, global bound = 7.01e-03, best block bound = 0.00e+00, Ibar >= max: True
    N= 64 lambda=+0.5: Ibar = 0.0228, kappa_N = 8.96, global bound = 6.25e-04, best block bound = 0.00e+00, Ibar >= max: True
    N= 64 lambda=+1.0: Ibar = 0.0819, kappa_N = 4.56, global bound = 1.74e-03, best block bound = 0.00e+00, Ibar >= max: True
    N= 64 lambda=+2.0: Ibar = 0.1734, kappa_N = 2.41, global bound = 3.91e-03, best block bound = 4.32e-05, Ibar >= max: True
    N= 64 lambda=+4.0: Ibar = 0.2468, kappa_N = 2.09, global bound = 6.94e-03, best block bound = 2.37e-04, Ibar >= max: True
    N= 64 lambda=-1.8: Ibar = 0.1580, kappa_N = 2.51, global bound = 3.51e-03, best block bound = 2.17e-05, Ibar >= max: True
  erratum check: with (J+h) instead of (J+|h|), h=-0.9, N=40, the 'global bound' would be 2.03 > 1
  lambda=0.5, E Ibar: N=50: 0.0241, N=100: 0.0198, N=200: 0.0172, N=400: 0.0165  (slowly converging in N)
  Khintchine: min_L<=400 E|sum_1^L r_i|/sqrt(L/2) = 1.000000 (>=1, Szarek), /sqrt(L/3) = 1.2247
=== E. Theorem thm:arealaw and the Slater lemma ===
  h(nu) <= 2 ln2 sqrt(nu(1-nu)) on 2e6 grid points: max(h - bound) = 0.00e+00 (<=0; equality at 1/2)
  d_1 = 0.1534 > 0, max_(2<=k<=2e5) d_k = -2.180e-09 (<0); ratio e_k/c_k decreasing: True
  Slater lemma (n=8, M=4, left/interior/non-contiguous A): spectrum err 7.8e-16, entropy err 2.2e-15, N_A law err 7.2e-16
  S <= 2ln2||P_B K P_A||_1: 9.1e-13;  ||.||_1 <= sum|K_xy|: -3.9e-16;  |K_xy| <= sum_z|U_xz||U_yz|: 0.0e+00 (all <=0)
  sum_z F(max(|x-z|,|y-z|)) <= 2 sum_(m>=ceil(d/2)) F(m): max violation = 4.4e-16 (<=0, up to truncation)
  E sup_t S(rho^q_A(t)) (N=60, lambda=2, CDW, l=30) = 1.690;  theorem bound 2ln2*Theta(F_emp) = 1.26e+03 <= 8ln2*M_2(F_emp) = 1.45e+03
  cross-check of the N=10 pipeline against ED (N=4): |S_full diff| = 2.2e-16, |S_f diff| = 4.4e-16
