=== G. Theorem thm:numberentropy ===
  Massey bound H(X) <= 1/2 ln(2 pi e (Var X + 1/12)) on random/binomial laws: max(H - bound) = -2.84e-03 (<=0)
  checks Var_q = sum|K_xy|^2, |<N_A>_q - |S cap A|| <= sum|U_xz|^2 <= sum Q: max violation = 3.7e-14
  N=64, lambda=2.0, CDW, A=[1,32], 400 sectors, t in [0,1e5]:
    S_N(t): max_t = 1.022, S_N(1e5) = 1.007;  Var_mix(N_A): max_t = 0.458
    Massey bound with the MEASURED variance (non-rigorous): max_t = 1.113
    E sup_t Var_q = 0.540 (<= K_1);  E sup_t (<N_A>_q - |S cap A|)^2 = 0.337 (<= K_2)
    theorem constant with F_emp (truncated at d<N): K_1 = Theta = 908, K_2 = Sigma'_1^2 = 9.48e+03, bound = 6.043
    with an exponential majorant F(d) = min(1, 1.00 e^(-0.181 d)) of F_emp, untruncated: K_1 = 1.4e+03, K_2 = 1.47e+04, bound = 6.264
    per-sector bound sup_t E_q S_N^q <= 1/2 ln(2 pi e (K_1 + 1/12)) = 4.825
